 systemd
# kio6 ships the kpasswdserver D-Bus service that credential autofill reads.
# Debian's libkf6kiocore6 symbols file already adds kio6 to ${shlibs:Depends}
# for anything linking KIO, so this is a restatement of intent rather than the
# thing that installs it -- kept so a change to that symbols file cannot
# silently drop the service, and weak because a host without it must still
# install and still mount with a hand-typed credential. Fedora, whose RPM
# requires are soname-based and pull only kf6-kio-core-libs, needs its own
# Recommends in the spec; there it is load-bearing.
Recommends: dolphin, kio6, plasma-systemsettings
Description: KDE Plasma CIFS mounts backed by static systemd units
 nasmount adds and removes persistent CIFS shares through a KAuth helper.
 Shares use root-owned systemd mount and automatic-mount unit pairs. They are
 armed at boot and exposed through a System Settings KCM and a Dolphin
 service-menu dialog.
 .
 The service-menu dialog fills in a credential this session already has for
 the share, through KDE's password service. Without that service running,
 credentials are simply typed by hand as before.
